+<h2>Optional picture analysis</h2>
+<p>For video projects, picture analysis is on by default and can be switched off before you accept the estimate. If enabled, we send a small silent copy of each video section, with timed transcript lines and an optional speaker count, to our processing service to help review speakers, shot changes, visible names and delivery. We do not use faces to name or identify people. Appearance is used only to judge whether a speaker is male or female (and roughly the age): a gender is set from the picture only when several clear sightings all agree, otherwise you are only told to check, and your own selected voice or gender is never changed. Temporary silent copies are removed when processing finishes, including handled errors. After an interrupted server process, temporary copies are removed during job cleanup. Anonymous text advice may be kept with the project; no face embeddings or separate face images are retained. Our processing service may keep request and response data under its own retention and safety rules.</p>
+
 <h2>How we use your information</h2>
 <ul>
   <li>To provide the dubbing service: transcription, translation, voice generation, and video merging.</li>
